    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lā^tro</span></b> , ōnis,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman surname.</i> So M. Porcius Latro, <i>a
				famous orator from Spain, a friend of the elder Seneca</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 1 praef.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 10,
				5, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 2,
			91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 14, 57, §
			160</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lătrō-nĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Latro, Latronian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">color,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 1, 7, 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1</span></i> praef.
			§ 13.</div>
